 # Elyon
-Erudas dad 
+
+An evidence broker and desktop browser verification host for **Response Provenance
++ Independent Inspection During Content Stalls**. Fresh implementation inspired by
+the usefulness of mobile inspection; no Eruda source or assets are included.
+
+This is executable desktop research, **not an iPhone browser or Gecko integration**.
+The broker preserves observations, explicit derivations, unknowns and capture gaps.
+It does not patch inspected Fetch/XHR or modify responses.
+
+## Run
+
+Python 3.12+; the broker itself has no third-party runtime dependencies.
+
+```sh
+python3 -m venv --system-site-packages .venv
+.venv/bin/python -m pip install -e '.[dev]'
+.venv/bin/python -m unittest discover -v
+.venv/bin/python -m mypy elyon
+.venv/bin/ruff check .
+.venv/bin/python -m build --no-isolation
+```
+
+The real-browser host requires `/usr/bin/chromium` and Playwright 1.62.0.
+Run it outside a nested command sandbox if the Chromium sandbox cannot initialize.
+Do not add `--no-sandbox` or disable browser policy to make it pass.
+
+```sh
+.venv/bin/python -m unittest validation.browser_check -v
+.venv/bin/python -m elyon.desktop --output artifacts/my-run --runs 100
+.venv/bin/python -m elyon.desktop --output artifacts/my-fixtures --fixtures
+```
+
+Use fresh output directories. These commands own and clean up their broker process,
+fixture server and browser. They leave a journal, evidence archive and report. The
+100-run host additionally writes a raw local snapshot and an export made during the
+stall. Local raw evidence may contain URLs; share the redacted archive instead.
+
+## Inspect without a browser
+
+The CLI is the milestone's inspection interface. No native UI is supplied.
+
+```sh
+.venv/bin/python -m elyon.cli serve --journal artifacts/manual/journal.ndjson \
+  --endpoint artifacts/manual/endpoint.json
+# In another terminal:
+.venv/bin/python -m elyon.cli command --endpoint artifacts/manual/endpoint.json \
+  '{"type":"hello"}'
+.venv/bin/python -m elyon.cli command --endpoint artifacts/manual/endpoint.json \
+  '{"type":"snapshot"}'
+.venv/bin/python -m elyon.cli command --endpoint artifacts/manual/endpoint.json \
+  '{"type":"export","redacted":true}' > artifacts/manual/export.json
+.venv/bin/python -m elyon.cli import artifacts/manual/export.json \
+  --journal artifacts/manual/imported.ndjson
+```
+
+Recorder state and capabilities are in `snapshot.captures` and `ready`; Requests
+are `RequestAttempt`/`ResponseVersion` nodes; Provenance consists of immutable nodes,
+relationships, source IDs, certainty, observation points and gaps; Export is a
+portable versioned JSON archive. Stop is a local command and never waits for content.
+The external adapter acknowledges `stopped` separately. The desktop harness performs
+the Start & Navigate stimulus; the broker never navigates inspected content itself.
+
+See [baseline](docs/BASELINE.md), [protocol](docs/PROTOCOL.md),
+[validation and limitations](docs/VALIDATION.md), and
+[native causal handoff gates](docs/CAUSAL_HANDOFF.md).
